  "note": "Gender classification as a skill: ending rules + ten/ta/to as the native probe + the A1 traps (people override endings; soft feminines flagged by badges). Uses only nouns taught by position 7.",
  "focus_structures": [
    "ten_ta_to"
  ],
  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "You decide gender every time",
      "title_pl": "Rodzaj wybierasz za każdym razem",
      "body": "Every Polish noun is masculine (m.), feminine (ż.) or neuter (n.) — and every adjective, and later every case ending, depends on it.\n\nThe endings tell you almost everything:",
      "body_pl": "Każdy rzeczownik ma rodzaj — i od niego zależy przymiotnik i końcówki.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Ending",
          "Gender",
          "Examples"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "consonant",
            "m. (masculine)",
            "dom · kot · sklep · stół"
          ],
          [
            "-a",
            "ż. (feminine)",
            "kawa · mama · kuchnia · woda"
          ],
          [
            "-o · -e · -um",
            "n. (neuter)",
            "piwo · morze · miasto · okno"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The native test: ten / ta / to",
      "title_pl": "Test: ten / ta / to",
      "body": "Poles check gender by trying \"this\": ten dom (m.) · ta kawa (ż.) · to piwo (n.) · te drzwi (plural).\n\nIf ten fits, it's masculine; ta — feminine; to — neuter. This unit drills that reflex.\n\nWatch the two to's: To jest piwo. = \"This is beer.\" (fixed frame) — but to piwo = \"this beer\" (gender test).",
      "body_pl": "Sprawdzasz przez „ten/ta/to\": ten dom · ta kawa · to piwo · te drzwi.\n\nUwaga: To jest piwo (rama) ≠ to piwo (wskazanie).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "this house",
          "pl": "ten dom"
        },
        {
          "en": "this coffee",
          "pl": "ta kawa"
        },
        {
          "en": "this beer",
          "pl": "to piwo"
        },
        {
          "en": "this door (plural in Polish)",
          "pl": "te drzwi"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The traps",
      "title_pl": "Pułapki",
      "body": "1. People override endings: tata and mężczyzna end in -a but are masculine — ten tata. Natural gender wins for people.\n\n2. Some consonant-ending nouns are feminine: mysz, noc, sól, twarz — you will meet them soon; the ż. badge marks every one. Nouns in -ość are ALWAYS feminine.\n\n3. A few nouns are plural-only: drzwi, and later spodnie, okulary, pieniądze — test with te, and they take są, not jest.",
      "body_pl": "1. Osoby: tata, mężczyzna = m. mimo -a.\n2. Niektóre spółgłoskowe są żeńskie: mysz, noc, sól, twarz (znaczek ż.); -ość zawsze ż.\n3. Tylko-mnogie: drzwi (te drzwi · są)."
    }
  ],
